1
00:02:55,555 --> 00:03:01,555
New friends. Old enemies.

2
00:05:51,111 --> 00:05:57,111
Wallace & Gromit: Vengeance Most Fowl is a family,
comedy, adventure film directed by Nick Park.

3
00:08:46,666 --> 00:08:52,666
Gromit’s concern that Wallace is becoming too dependent on his inventions proves justified,
when Wallace invents a “smart” gnome that seems to develop a mind of its own.

4
00:11:42,222 --> 00:11:48,222
When it emerges that a vengeful figure from the past might be masterminding things, it falls to Gromit to
battle sinister forces and save his master… or Wallace may never be able to invent again!

5
00:14:37,777 --> 00:14:43,777
Wallace (voice), played by Ben Whitehead.

6
00:17:33,333 --> 00:17:39,333
Chief Inspector Mackintosh (voice), played by Peter Kay.

7
00:20:28,888 --> 00:20:34,888
P.C. Mukherjee (voice), played by Lauren Patel.

8
00:23:24,444 --> 00:23:30,444
Norbot (voice), played by Reece Shearsmith.

9
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Onya Doorstep (voice), played by Diane Morgan.

10
00:29:15,555 --> 00:29:21,555
Judge (voice), played by Adjoa Andoh.

11
00:32:11,111 --> 00:32:17,111
Wallace & Gromit: Vengeance Most Fowl is a 2024 British animated comedy
film produced by Aardman Animations for the BBC and Netflix.

12
00:35:06,666 --> 00:35:12,666
The sixth instalment in the Wallace & Gromit series and the second to be feature-length following The Curse of the
Were-Rabbit (2005), it was directed by Nick Park and Merlin Crossingham and written by Park and Mark Burton.

13
00:38:02,222 --> 00:38:08,222
In the film, Wallace's latest invention is hijacked by a vengeful Feathers
McGraw; it serves as a sequel to The Wrong Trousers (1993).

14
00:40:57,777 --> 00:41:03,777
Ben Whitehead voices Wallace in his first feature-length appearance
following the death of original voice actor Peter Sallis in 2017.

15
00:43:53,333 --> 00:43:59,333
The remaining voice cast consists of Peter Kay,
Lauren Patel, and Reece Shearsmith.

16
00:46:48,888 --> 00:46:54,888
Owing to difficulties with working with DreamWorks Animation during the production of The Curse of the
Were-Rabbit, Park was hesitant on directing another feature-length Wallace & Gromit film for several years.

17
00:49:44,444 --> 00:49:50,444
Vengeance Most Fowl, which was announced in January 2022, with Park and Crossingham attached as directors, and Burton
as screenwriter, was initially conceived as another 30-minute short, before expanding into a feature.

18
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:46,000
The score was composed by Lorne Balfe and series composer Julian Nott.

19
00:55:35,555 --> 00:55:41,555
Wallace & Gromit: Vengeance Most Fowl premiered at the
American Film Institute on 27 October 2024.

20
00:58:31,111 --> 00:58:37,111
It was broadcast on BBC One and BBC iPlayer on 25 December in the UK and
was released on Netflix internationally on 3 January 2025.

21
01:01:26,666 --> 01:01:32,666
After 28 days of catch-up viewing, it became the BBC's
most watched scripted show since 2002.

22
01:04:22,222 --> 01:04:28,222
The film received critical acclaim, holding a 100% rating on
the review aggregator website Rotten Tomatoes.

23
01:07:17,777 --> 01:07:23,777
It was nominated in the Animated Feature categories at the Academy Awards, Golden
Globe Awards, Annie Awards and the BAFTAs, winning the latter.

24
01:10:13,333 --> 01:10:19,333
It also won the inaugural BAFTA Award for Best Children's & Family Film, in addition
to being nominated for Outstanding British Film at the same ceremony.

25
01:13:08,888 --> 01:13:14,888
The film explores themes of inventor, human animal
relationship, penguin, anthropomorphism, revenge.

26
01:16:04,444 --> 01:16:10,444
The tone is lighthearted.
